course: dictionary
lesson: 7671
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word prophet is a good example. «Prophets were messengers who spoke God's word: they warned kings and people about injustice.» Here a prophet is someone chosen by God to bring a message, not someone guessing the weather.
explain: The same word can change its meaning in a new sentence. «She is a prophet of doom, always saying the bus will be late.» Doom means bad luck or disaster, so a prophet of doom is someone who always predicts bad things. Nobody here is talking about religion.
explain: Ask yourself: is this sentence about faith, about the future, or about a person being bad luck? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A prophet is a person who people believe is chosen by God to bring a message or tell the future.
fact: A prophet can also be someone who predicts what will happen.
fact: With a capital P, the Prophet usually means a central religious figure, such as the Prophet Muhammad in Islam.
fact: In religious education, prophets appear in Judaism, Christianity and Islam, for example Moses, Isaiah and Muhammad.
fact: In everyday talk, «a prophet of doom» is someone who always predicts bad things.
exercise: «Prophets were messengers who spoke God's word.» In this sentence, what is a prophet? | A king who rules a faraway land | A poet who writes about the sea | A shopkeeper at a market | *A person chosen by God to bring a message
exercise: «He is a prophet of doom, always saying the bus will be late.» What does prophet of doom mean? | A religious leader who travels far | A person who never tells the time | *Someone who always predicts bad things | Someone who always makes people laugh
exercise: Ben reads, «The Prophet Muhammad lived in Arabia about 1,400 years ago.» Which meaning of prophet fits here? | *A central religious figure in Islam | A teacher who marks spelling tests | A weather forecaster on the television
test: «The prophet Nathan said, "You are the man!" to King David.» What is Nathan? | A cook who worked in the palace | A king who gave orders to his people | *A messenger who brought God's word to a king
test: Which meaning of prophet fits Lily's sentence, «Grandma says the rain will stop by noon, she is a prophet»? | *Someone who predicts what will happen | A religious figure in Islam | A messenger chosen by God | A person who sells grain
exam: Read «The prophet Nathan warned King David about his sin.» Which meaning of prophet is used? | A person who sells food at a market | A dog that guards a house | *A person who brings a message from God and warns people | A person who never speaks in class
